sion of  Tomb Raider it still handles the game  quite well with high settings at 1080p  staying well above 30 frames per second  though the difference is only noticeable  on occasion the office stands above the  Xbox one so far as titanfall is  concerned the Alpha struggled a bit with  watchdogs on high settings so we had to  dial the effects down a bit to hit a  reasonable frame rate at 1080p still  next to the PlayStation 4 version it's  hard to notice any major differences  Middle Earth shadow of Mordor could have  ran closer to 60 frames per second on  the Alpha with more conservative  settings but alien where's little blocks  stayed above 30 frames per second when  we turned on advanced stuff like ambient  occlusion  tesselation remaining totally playable  while looking good too these tests make  it clear that the Alpha is on average as  capable as PlayStation 4 and Xbox one  when it comes to sheer in-game  performance unlike those systems the  alphas RAM and CPU are upgradeable if  you spend a little more money you can  push the alpha further than we have in  our tests but at that point at about  $850  it may be worth investing in a  traditional PC with a stronger GPU  although some people refer to the Alpha  as a console it's driven by Microsoft  Windows a PC operating system and with  that the Alpha exhibits the same general  capabilities and limitations as any  other Windows gaming PC what is unique  about the Alpha and why some consider to  be a console is iliyan where's custom  user interface which boots up on top of  Windows and is 100% controller friendly  currently the Alpha has only integrated  valve scheme service within the UI this  is because steams big picture mode makes  it easy to access the marketplace in  your own library of games with only a  controller either EA's origin or  Ubisoft's you play touts a controller  friendly interface and while they are  still accessible through the alphas  Windows 8.1 desktop mode there is no way  to properly 